 0/height/667/33171_stine-an-headshot.rev.1792517747.jpg" title="Stine An H
 eadshot" srcset="https://events.iu.edu/live/image/scale/2x/gid/429/width/5
 00/height/667/33171_stine-an-headshot.rev.1792517747.jpg 2x\, https://even
 ts.iu.edu/live/image/scale/3x/gid/429/width/500/height/667/33171_stine-an-
 headshot.rev.1792517747.jpg 3x" data-max-w="2000" data-max-h="2667" loadin
 g="lazy" data-optimized="true"/></picture> Stine An is a poet\, translator
 \, and performer based in New York City. She holds a BA in Literature from
  Harvard and an MFA in Literary Arts from Brown\, and has received fellows
 hips and grants from The Poetry Project\, the PEN/Heim Translation Fund Gr
 ant\, Yaddo\, ALTA\, and the National Endowment for the Arts. Her publicat
 ions include <i data-ogsc="">Today's Morning Vocabulary</i> by Yoo Heekyun
 g (2025)\, <i data-ogsc="">Winter Night Rabbit Worries </i>by Yoo Heekyung
  (2026)\, and <i data-ogsc="">S_MMER CR_SH</i> (2025). Their debut poetry 
 collection\, <i data-ogsc="">B-Dragon Suite</i> (2026)\, won the 2023 Nigh
 tboat Poetry Prize and is available from Nightboat Books. You can find her
  online at <a title="Original URL: http://gregorspamsa.com/. Click or tap 
 if you trust this link." href="https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.
 com/?url=http:%2F%2Fgregorspamsa.com%2F&amp\;data=05%7C02%7Cmcalver%40iu.e
