SUMMARY:Mike Mattner\, clarinet\; Kimberly Carballo\, piano
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy this performance from almost anywhere in the world viaL
 IVE@jacobs!Featuring  Eric Bowling\, flute (alumnus guest)  Jacob Burk\, 
 violaSara Dailey\, narrator (alumna guest)&#160\;Helen Ford\, cello (gues
 t)  Michael Grubb\, narrator (guest)  Maria Izzo Walker\, soprano (alumna
  guest)  Emily Nehus\, violin (alumna guest)  Paulina Villarreal\, mezzo-
 soprano/narrator  RepertoireChappell Kingsland: Confessions of a Murderes
 s (2003/10)Anthony Plog: Animal Ditties I (1978)Daniel Cueto: Ave (2025/2
 6\, premiere)Elaine Fine: Happy Family (2005)Jenni Brandon: The Woman wit
 h the Unfathomable Eyes (2010)About the Artists  Clarinetist Mike Mattner
  (M.M. University of Colorado\, Boulder\; B.Mus.Ed. Crane School of Music
 -SUNY Potsdam) has enjoyed a teaching and performing career spanning 34 y
 ears. He is a former member of the Midland Symphony\, Boulder MahlerFest 
 Orchestra\, Philharmonia à Vent\, Orion Winds\, Bloomington Pops\, Bloom
 ington Symphony\, Class Act Productions\, Houston Repertoire Ballet\, The
  Woodlands Concert Band\, and the Woodland Winds Quintet\, and has perfor
 med in numerous musical theater productions. He currently performs with t
 he Bloomington Symphony Orchestra\, the Southern Indiana Wind Ensemble\, 
 Reimagining Opera for Kids\, Voces Novae\, and several chamber music ense
 mbles.Kimberly Carballo serves in the Indiana University Jacobs School of
  Music as Director of Jacobs Virtual Academy (JVA) and as teaching profes
 sor in the Chamber Music and Collaborative Piano department. Carballo is 
 also an active international performer and educator\, teaching both at th
 e university and in her private studio. She is a strong believer in and p
 racticer of community engagement locally and globally. She founded Reimag
 ining Opera for Kids (ROK)\, a music Bloomington-based community engageme
 nt and education program\, participates annually as faculty advisor for t
 he IU portion of the team in the Cheerful Heart Music Education Mission i
 n the Dominican Republic and Haiti\, and is a founding member of the Amit
 y Trio\, a chamber ensemble that commissions and performs new music to am
 plify underrepresented voices.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Enjoy this performance from almos
 t anywhere in the world via</strong><a href="https://liveatjacobs.music.i
 ndiana.edu/"><strong>LIVE@jacobs</strong></a><strong>!<br /></strong></p>
 <p><strong>Featuring</strong><br />  Eric Bowling\, flute (alumnus guest)
 <br />  Jacob Burk\, viola<strong><br /></strong>Sara Dailey\, narrator (
 alumna guest)&#160\;<strong><br /></strong>Helen Ford\, cello (guest)<br 
 />  Michael Grubb\, narrator (guest)<br />  Maria Izzo Walker\, soprano (
 alumna guest)<br />  Emily Nehus\, violin (alumna guest)<br />  Paulina V
 illarreal\, mezzo-soprano/narrator<br /><strong><br />  Repertoire<br /><
 /strong>Chappell Kingsland: <em>Confessions of a Murderess (2003/10)<br /
 ></em>Anthony Plog: <em>Animal Ditties I (1978)<br /></em>Daniel Cueto: <
 em>Ave (2025/26\, premiere)<br /></em>Elaine Fine: <em>Happy Family (2005
 )<br /></em>Jenni Brandon: <em>The Woman with the Unfathomable Eyes (2010
 )<br /></em><br /><strong>About the Artists</strong><br /><br />  Clarine
 tist <strong>Mike Mattner</strong> (M.M. University of Colorado\, Boulder
 \; B.Mus.Ed. Crane School of Music-SUNY Potsdam) has enjoyed a teaching a
 nd performing career spanning 34 years. He is a former member of the Midl
 and Symphony\, Boulder MahlerFest Orchestra\, Philharmonia à Vent\, Orio
 n Winds\, Bloomington Pops\, Bloomington Symphony\, Class Act Productions
 \, Houston Repertoire Ballet\, The Woodlands Concert Band\, and the Woodl
 and Winds Quintet\, and has performed in numerous musical theater product
 ions. He currently performs with the Bloomington Symphony Orchestra\, the
  Southern Indiana Wind Ensemble\, Reimagining Opera for Kids\, Voces Nova
 e\, and several chamber music ensembles.<br /><br /><strong>Kimberly Carb
 allo</strong> serves in the Indiana University Jacobs School of Music as 
 Director of Jacobs Virtual Academy (JVA) and as teaching professor in the
  Chamber Music and Collaborative Piano department. Carballo is also an ac
 tive international performer and educator\, teaching both at the universi
 ty and in her private studio. She is a strong believer in and practicer o
 f community engagement locally and globally. She founded Reimagining Oper
 a for Kids (ROK)\, a music Bloomington-based community engagement and edu
 cation program\, participates annually as faculty advisor for the IU port
 ion of the team in the Cheerful Heart Music Education Mission in the Domi
 nican Republic and Haiti\, and is a founding member of the Amity Trio\, a
  chamber ensemble that commissions and performs new music to amplify unde
 rrepresented voices.</p>
