CREATED:20261028T183346Z
DESCRIPTION:<br>🏫 Join us for a Visitors Day to learn more about the Ha
 rmony School experience! Parents will hear an introduction by Steve “Roc
 ” Bonchek\, Executive Director\, followed by a tour through the building
 \, and ending with an opportunity to speak with your child’s potential t
 eachers. During this time\, prospective students aged 6 and up can visit a
  classroom.<br><br>While Visitors Day is best suited for children ages 6 a
 nd older to attend\, we’d love to introduce your little one to our Early
  Childhood Program (ECP)! We’re happy to set up a personalized tour for 
 children under the age of 6 after families attend Visitors Day.<br><br>
 📅Our next Visitors Day will be held on Tuesday\, November 10th. The sch
 edule is as follows:<br>11:00 AM: Introduction &amp\; Tour (Roc\, Director
 )<br>11:45 AM: Classroom Observation<br>12:00 PM: Teacher Meet &amp\; Gree
 t<br><br>Please RSVP at <a href="https://www.harmonyschool.org/visitorsday
 ?fbclid=IwZXh0bgNhZW0CMTAAcGRvZgFicmlkETF4YUZUMU52TE85dVdHbEh2c3J0YwZhcHBf
 aWQQMjIyMDM5MTc4ODIwMDg5MgABHyw78hlfFFWW8gvOKvHRPWOezUW9WdAwSr8Y0WVn5ET-A_
 pxHD-r0XJzLwpw_aem_8Rd3mfBWS68nqVyh0HAcpQ" target="_blank">https://www.har
 monyschool.org/visitorsday</a>. RSVP isn’t required but it is appreciate
 d for planning purposes.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261102T184553Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Harmony School Calendar
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"WFHB Community Calendar": "https://wfhb.org/events/harmonys-visitors-day/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_d1087e97d4ace1c1ca2dd6336d417bea870ddac277be6d1711cbc0235aa85228
SUMMARY:Harmony's Visitors Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261110T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261110T140000
DTSTAMP:20261107T055250Z
UID:mu1o622chv6jn70hct7bkv4f3s@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261110T110000
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261102T190657Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Do you want to learn more about Harmony School? Harmony Sch
 ool invites prospective parents and students to discover how its small cla
 ss sizes and creative approach to learning nurture each child's heart\, mi
 nd\, and voice.</p>\n<p>Parents will hear an introduction by Steve "Roc" B
 onchek\, Executive Director\, followed by a tour of the building and a cha
 nce to speak with your child's potential teachers. Prospective students ag
 ed 6 and up can visit a classroom.</p>\n<p><b>Schedule</b><br>11:00 AM: In
 troduction and Tour (Roc\, Director)<br>11:45 AM: Classroom Observation<br
 >12:00 PM: Teacher Meet and Greet</p>\n<p><b>Children under 6:</b> Visitor
 s Day is best suited for children ages 6 and older. Harmony is happy to se
 t up a personalized tour of its Early Childhood Program (ECP) for children
  under 6 after families attend Visitors Day.</p>\n<p><b>RSVP:</b> Not requ
 ired\, but appreciated for planning purposes. <a href="https://form.jotfor
 m.com/263015060797154">Register for Visitors Day</a></p>\n<p><b>Questions:
 </b> (812) 334-8349 or info@harmonyschool.org</p>\n<p>Listed on Bloomingto
 nOnline.com\, your community guide to Bloomington and Monroe County\, Indi
 ana.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20261102T190657Z
LOCATION:Harmony School\, 909 E 2nd St\, Bloomington\, IN
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-SOURCE:BloomingtonOnline Events, WFHB Community Calendar
END:VEVENT
