DTSTART:20261110T210000Z
DTEND:20261110T220000Z
LOCATION:MAXWELL HALL
GEO:39.16705;-86.524718
SUMMARY:Climates of Change: Past\, Present\, Future
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for an interdisciplinary conversation on "Clim
 ate of Change: Past\, Present\, Future" that explores how people have exp
 erienced\, understood\, and responded to changing climates across time. F
 rom the environmental disruptions of the premodern past to the cultural a
 nd political challenges of the present and the choices shaping our future
 \, the speakers will consider how deep reflection on the inevitability of
  change might help us approach precarious climate futures. The event will
  feature brief comments by Shannon Gayk (English and Environmental Future
 s)\, Christopher Callahan (O'Neill)\, Suzannah Comfort (Media School)\, a
 nd Shane Greene (Anthropology).
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Please join us for an interdisciplinary
  conversation on "<em>Climate of Change: Past\, Present\, Future"</em> th
 at explores how people have experienced\, understood\, and responded to c
 hanging climates across time. From the environmental disruptions of the p
 remodern past to the cultural and political challenges of the present and
  the choices shaping our future\, the speakers will consider how deep ref
 lection on the inevitability of change might help us approach precarious 
 climate futures. The event will feature brief comments by Shannon Gayk (E
 nglish and Environmental Futures)\, Christopher Callahan (O'Neill)\, Suza
 nnah Comfort (Media School)\, and Shane Greene (Anthropology).</p>
