 ill.indiana.edu/faculty-research/directory/profiles/faculty/full-time/ziro
 giannis-nikolaos.html">Nikos Zirogiannis</a> (O'Neill School) and five oth
 er IUB faculty members as they share the one thing you need to know about 
 climate change.</p><p><a href="https://oneill.indiana.edu/faculty-research
 /directory/profiles/faculty/full-time/callahan-christopher.html">Christoph
 er Callahan</a> (O'Neill)\, <a href="https://folklore.indiana.edu/about/fa
 culty/dirksen-rebecca.html">Rebecca Dirksen</a> (Folklore &amp\; Ethnomusi
 cology)\, <a href="https://history.indiana.edu/faculty_staff/faculty/gregg
 _sara.html">Sara Gregg</a> (History)\, <a href="https://oneill.indiana.edu
 /faculty-research/directory/profiles/faculty/full-time/novick-kimberly.htm
 l">Kim Novick</a> (O'Neill and <a href="https://environment.indiana.edu/in
 dex.html">ESSI</a>)\, and <a href="https://education.indiana.edu/news/2026
 /jul-dec/2026-08-20-iusoe-welcomes-new-faculty.html">Spencer Perry</a> (Sc
 hool of Education) will each share five minutes of what they want us to kn
 ow about climate change.</p><p>  These talks will be followed by discussio
 n and Q&amp\;A. This event is sponsored by IU's <a href="https://ias.india
 na.edu/">Institute for Advanced Study</a>. All IU and Bloomington communit
 y members are invited to attend and learn with us during this <a href="htt
 ps://eri.iu.edu/news-and-events/events/iu-climate-week.html">IU Climate We
 ek</a> event.</p>
