SUMMARY:Homeschool Day: Tabletop Treasures (PM Session)
DTSTART:20261112T180000Z
DTEND:20261112T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260716T121535Z
UID:20261112T180000Z-2352812@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261112T180000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1081,1081/31448_HSD-FullColor.rev.1783430812.png
DESCRIPTION:Students will look closely at still life paintings in the gall
 eries\, discovering how artists use symbolism and lighting to communicate 
 mood and reveal more than meets the eye. After finding inspiration in the 
 galleries\, students will create their own still life paintings by arrangi
 ng and observing objects at their table to tell their own unique stories! 
  Program designed by our licensed art educator for students in grades K-12
 .Know Before You Go:  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education on the 2
 nd floor of the museum at 1 pm. Together\, we'll drop off personal items b
 efore exploring the galleries. After seeing artworks that will inspire our
  project\, we'll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create
  our own masterpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!  Strollers are we
 lcome. Chaperone required. We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with on
 e adult for every 6 children.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20260716T161535Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2344750-homeschool-day-tabletop-trea
 sures-pm-session
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Students will look closely at still life
  paintings in the galleries\, discovering how artists use symbolism and li
 ghting to communicate mood and reveal more than meets the eye. After findi
 ng inspiration in the galleries\, students will create their own still lif
 e paintings by arranging and observing objects at their table to tell thei
 r own unique stories!</p><p>  Program designed by our licensed art educato
 r for students in grades K-12.</p><p><strong>Know Before You Go:</strong><
 /p><p>  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of th
 e museum at 1 pm. Together\, we'll drop off personal items before explorin
 g the galleries. After seeing artworks that will inspire our project\, we'
 ll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our own maste
 rpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!</p><p>  Strollers are welcome. 
 <strong>Chaperone required.</strong> We ask that chaperones be 18 or older
 \, with one adult for every 6 children.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  <strong>Madelyn Cage</strong><br />\n  You
 th and Family Art Education Manager<br />\n  Sidney and Lois Eskenazi Muse
 um of Art<br />\n  <a href="mailto:cagem@iu.edu">cagem@iu.edu<br />\n  812
 -855-0607</a>\n</p>
