X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Arts & Humanities Institute": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2463756-clacs-faculty-research-symposium-with-luciana", "IU Hamilton Lugar School": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2463756-clacs-faculty-research-symposium-with-luciana"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 130": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2463756-clacs-faculty-research-symposium-with-luciana"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_130
SUMMARY:CLACS Faculty Research Symposium with Luciana Namorato
DTSTART:20261112T180000Z
DTEND:20261112T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261103T094733Z
UID:20261112T180000Z-2471899@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261112T180000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/137/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,2013,2013/33266_Namorato1.rev.1793042712.jpg
CATEGORIES:Culture and languages,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conference
 s
DESCRIPTION:The Center for Latin American and Caribbean Studies (CLACS) we
 lcomes Dr. Luciana Namorato for The Other Fridas: Hidden Voices\, New Hist
 ories &amp\; Future Agendas of Latin American Women Artists\, part of the 
 Fall 2026 CLACS Faculty Research Symposium.  Thursday\, November 12th| 1-2
 PM | Hamilton Lugar School GA2134  This presentation explores the recognit
 ion and representation of Latin American women artists\, considering how t
 heir voices and experiences can expand our understanding of the region's a
 rtistic histories.  Dr. Namorato is an associate professor in the Departme
 nt of Spanish and Portuguese and co-editor of The Other Fridas: The Lives 
 and Works of Latin American Women Artists. Her research includes Brazilian
  and Portuguese literature\, gender studies\, and contemporary Latin Ameri
 can literature.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261103T144733Z
LOCATION:Hamilton Lugar School
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2463756-clacs-faculty-research-sympo
 sium-with-luciana
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">  The Center for La
 tin American and Caribbean Studies (CLACS) welcomes Dr. <strong>Luciana Na
 morato</strong> for <strong><em>The Other Fridas: Hidden Voices\, New Hist
 ories &amp\; Future Agendas of Latin American Women Artists</em></strong>\
 , part of the Fall 2026 CLACS Faculty Research Symposium.</p><p data-pm-sl
 ice="1 1 []">  Thursday\, November 12th| 1-2PM | Hamilton Lugar School GA2
 134</p><p>  This presentation explores the recognition and representation 
 of Latin American women artists\, considering how their voices and experie
 nces can expand our understanding of the region's artistic histories.</p><
 p>  Dr. Namorato is an associate professor in the Department of Spanish an
 d Portuguese and co-editor of <em>The Other Fridas: The Lives and Works of
  Latin American Women Artists</em>. Her research includes Brazilian and Po
