X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Mathers Museum of World Cultures": "https://events.iu.edu/iumaa/event/storytelling-at-the-museum-2026", "WFHB Community Calendar": "https://wfhb.org/events/storytelling-at-the-museum/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 353": "https://events.iu.edu/iumaa/event/storytelling-at-the-museum-2026"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_353
X-SOURCE:IU Mathers Museum of World Cultures, WFHB Community Calendar
DTSTART:20261112T223000Z
DTEND:20261113T003000Z
LOCATION:IU Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology\, 416 N. Indiana Ave.\
 , Bloomington\, IN 47408
GEO:39.170023;-86.526132
SUMMARY:Storytelling at the Museum
DESCRIPTION:Event Details:      This program has a little bit of everythi
 ng for booklovers and storytellers!    Take home a custom typewriter poem
  from the Bloomington Writer's Guild or try your hand at typing one yours
 elf!      Feeling inspired by poetry? Create a tiny keepsake with our pic
 ture frame poetry craft!      Make a book nook to liven up your bookshelv
 es and decorate a bookplate to add to your favorite novel.      Intereste
 d in the ancient art of writing and storytelling? Make your own cuneiform
  tablet out of clay!      Snack on some gourmet cookies and pies while ge
 tting your creativity flowing.            This program is free and open t
 o all\, with Museum galleries remaining open for the entirety of the even
 t to give a special\, after-hours view of the exhibitions.    &#160\;Park
 ing Information:  Limited complimentary parking is available in front of 
 the Museum entrance (https://maps.app.goo.gl/k4Txsojst2gSW5fUA) off India
 na Avenue. Free street parking is available in surrounding neighborhoods 
 on weekends and weekdays after 5:00 PM.  Paid parking is also available i
 n the University Collections at McCalla (https://maps.app.goo.gl/3i62KNcj
 DeCACruHA) parking lot off Indiana Avenue and the Indiana Memorial Union 
 (https://maps.app.goo.gl/2n49VoLuF78o5twJA) visitor lot.  Metered street 
 parking is available near Sample Gates and throughout downtown Bloomingto
 n\, including along Kirkwood Avenue\, East 6th Street\, East 4th Street\,
  North Lincoln Street\, North Dunn Street\, and South Grant Street.Questi
 ons?  For accessibility assistance or questions about this event\, please
  reach out to Camden Hill at camrhill@iu.edu (mailto:camrhill@iu.edu) or 
 (812) 855-1696.Note:  By attending this event\, you agree to be in photog
 raphy that may be used by the University for promotional purposes. If you
  would not like to be in any pictures\, please speak to a Museum staff me
 mber and they will inform assigned photographers of your request. If you 
 see that your image has been used in error\, please reach out to iumaa@iu
 .edu (mailto:iumaa@iu.edu) to request that it be taken down.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Event Details:</strong></p><div c
 lass="ewa-rteLine"><div class="ewa-rteLine"><p>      This program has a l
 ittle bit of everything for booklovers and storytellers!    </p><ul><li>T
 ake home a custom typewriter poem from the Bloomington Writer's Guild or 
 try your hand at typing one yourself!      </li><li>Feeling inspired by p
 oetry? Create a tiny keepsake with our picture frame poetry craft!      <
 /li><li>Make a book nook to liven up your bookshelves and decorate a book
 plate to add to your favorite novel.      </li><li>Interested in the anci
 ent art of writing and storytelling? Make your own cuneiform tablet out o
 f clay!      </li><li>Snack on some gourmet cookies and pies while gettin
 g your creativity flowing.      </li></ul><p>      This program is free a
 nd open to all\, with Museum galleries remaining open for the entirety of
  the event to give a special\, after-hours view of the exhibitions.    </
 p></div>&#160\;</div><p><strong>Parking Information:</strong></p><p data-
 pm-slice="1 1 []">  Limited complimentary parking is available in front o
 f the <a class="external" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/k4Txsojst2gSW5fUA
 ">Museum entrance</a> off Indiana Avenue. Free street parking is availabl
 e in surrounding neighborhoods on weekends and weekdays after 5:00 PM.</p
 ><p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">  Paid parking is also available in the <a cla
 ss="external" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/3i62KNcjDeCACruHA">University
  Collections at McCalla</a> parking lot off Indiana Avenue and the <a cla
 ss="external" href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/2n49VoLuF78o5twJA">Indiana Me
 morial Union</a> visitor lot.</p><p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">  Metered stre
 et parking is available near Sample Gates and throughout downtown Bloomin
 gton\, including along Kirkwood Avenue\, East 6th Street\, East 4th Stree
 t\, North Lincoln Street\, North Dunn Street\, and South Grant Street.</p
 ><p data-ogsc="black"><strong>Questions?</strong></p><p data-ogsc="black"
 >  For accessibility assistance or questions about this event\, please re
 ach out to Camden Hill at <a href="mailto:camrhill@iu.edu" target="_blank
 " rel="noopener noreferrer">camrhill@iu.edu</a> or (812) 855-1696.</p><p 
 data-ogsc="black"><strong>Note:</strong></p><p data-ogsc="black">  By att
 ending this event\, you agree to be in photography that may be used by th
 e University for promotional purposes. If you would not like to be in any
  pictures\, please speak to a Museum staff member and they will inform as
 signed photographers of your request. If you see that your image has been
  used in error\, please reach out to <a href="mailto:iumaa@iu.edu">iumaa@
 iu.edu</a> to request that it be taken down.</p>
