BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Campuslabs Iub": "https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12953594"}
X-SOURCE-ID:campuslabs_iub
X-SOURCE:IU beINvolved Student Orgs
CATEGORIES:GroupBusiness
CATEGORIES:Academic/Career
DESCRIPTION: \nStudying & Working Abroad: A Faculty Panel\nWhat does an in
 ternational academic and professional career actually look like? Join EBA
  for an evening with three Kelley professors whose careers have crossed b
 orders.\n\nProfessor Sridhar Arcot went from the London School of Economi
 cs to fifteen years at ESSEC in Paris\, where he was Academic Director of
  the MSc in Finance. He now co-directs Kelley’s Capital Markets & Banking
  Workshop.\nProfessor Francesco Marchionne built his academic and profess
 ional career across Ancona\, Turin and Nottingham before coming to Bloomi
 ngton. His class trips to Italy have inspired many students to study abro
 ad.\nProfessor Andreas Hauskrecht started at Freie Universität Berlin and
  has spent more than three decades advising Vietnam’s government and cent
 ral bank. He has also advised central banks in Bolivia\, Ecuador\, Laos a
 nd Moldova.\n\nWe’ll talk about choosing between European and US programs
 \, building a career that spans countries\, and how to make a semester or
  job abroad count. After the moderated discussion\, the floor is open for
  your questions. You can stay afterwards for informal networking with the
  panelists.\nWhether you’re an international student planning your next s
 tep or an American student thinking about Europe\, this panel is for you.
  All majors welcome.\n\nHosted by: European Business Association\n\nAddit
 ional Information can be found at: https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/1
 2953594
DTEND:20261113T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20261107T055320Z
DTSTART:20261112T233000Z
LOCATION:IMU Oak Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Panel discussion with Professors of European background
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12953594
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12953594
X-HOSTS:European Business Association
END:VEVENT
