ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/11/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,768,768/32784_260911_CAMi_Promotional_Image_05-detail-WEB.
 rev.1790774789.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:Opening reception: Friday\, October 2\, 2026\, 6–10pm  Exhib
 ition on view: October 2–December 18\, 2026  For this exhibition\, the b
 lueprint is used as both a representational and conceptual departure point
 . Daniel Luis Martinez uses cyanotype printmaking and mixed-media drawing 
 techniques as a generative process to imagine a speculative home on the CA
 Mi campus. The hybrid drawings and prints featured in the exhibition explo
 re the tactile middle-ground of the blueprint as a creative endeavor.  The
  series employs orthographic conventions typical of architectural drawing 
 sets\, though not as precise instructions for building. Rather\, a layered
  and loose approach expresses ideas of home as an architectonic language. 
  Daniel Luis Martinez is a registered architect\, educator\, and co-founde
 r of the multi-disciplinary design studio LAA Office\, which explores the 
 intersection of landscape\, art\, and architecture. His research and creat
 ive work investigate the potential of public art to generate alternative f
 orms of placemaking. Martinez is Associate Professor and Director of the I
 U Eskenazi School's J. Irwin Miller Architecture Program (https://architec
 ture.indiana.edu/index.html) in Columbus\, Indiana.  Learn more about the 
 exhibition at the CAMI website (https://camindy.org/exhibitions-all/theblu
 eprint).
GEO:39.72915;-86.138756
LAST-MODIFIED:20260930T134621Z
LOCATION:The Contemporary Art Museum of Indianapolis
URL:https://events.iu.edu/soaadiub/event/2435603-daniel-luis-martinez-the-
 blueprint-exhibition
