SUMMARY:Open Studio
DTSTART:20261118T180000Z
DTEND:20261118T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260519T102933Z
UID:20261111T180000Z-2303411@events.iu.edu__20261118
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,3200,2134/2693_2I1A0095_1.rev.1573483976.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Health and wellness
DESCRIPTION:Our Open Studio program invites participants to create in the 
 museum's art studio\, where art becomes a tool for reflection\, expression
 \, and connection. Guided by a trained art therapist\, the open studio wel
 comes visitors to engage with materials at their own pace while drawing in
 spiration from the surrounding exhibitions. No art experience is needed\; 
 just bring your curiosity and a desire to create\, and we'll handle the re
 st!  Participants are welcome to utilize supplies located in the studio\, 
 as well as bring their own supplies/projects to work on.  This group meets
  on the 2nd and 4th Wednesday of every month\, excluding holidays and muse
 um closures. It is open to everyone: students\, staff\, and the public inc
 luded! The group will meet in the Roehm Family Art-making Studio\, located
  inside the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the Eskenazi 
 Museum of Art.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20260519T142933Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2298120-open-studio
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Our Open Studio program invites particip
 ants to create in the museum's art studio\, where art becomes a tool for r
 eflection\, expression\, and connection. Guided by a trained art therapist
 \, the open studio welcomes visitors to engage with materials at their own
  pace while drawing inspiration from the surrounding exhibitions. No art e
 xperience is needed\; just bring your curiosity and a desire to create\, a
 nd we'll handle the rest!</p><p>  Participants are welcome to utilize supp
 lies located in the studio\, as well as bring their own supplies/projects 
 to work on.</p><p>  This group meets on the 2nd and 4th Wednesday of every
  month\, excluding holidays and museum closures. It is open to everyone: s
 tudents\, staff\, and the public included! The group will meet in the Roeh
 m Family Art-making Studio\, located inside the Simpson Center for Educati
 on on the 2nd floor of the Eskenazi Museum of Art.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<div>\n  <strong>Keaton Evans-Black\, LMHC\, ATR<
 /strong>\n</div>\n<div>\n  <i>Arts-Based Wellness Experiences Manager</i>\
 n</div>\n<div>\n  Sidney and Lois Eskenazi Museum of Art\n</div>\n<div>\n 
  Indiana University\n</div>\n<div>\n  kevansbl@iu.edu\, (812) 855-5942\n</
 div>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
