X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_130
SUMMARY:The Declaration of Independence: The Motives\, the Moment
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
DTSTAMP:20260109T131533Z
UID:20261107T050000Z-2300399@events.iu.edu__20261120
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,288,288/31279_declaration_title_LW_graphic.rev.1781630899
 .png
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:The Declaration of Independence: The Motives\, The Momentexami
 nes a crucial time in American history through the collections of the Lill
 y Library. The first printing of the Declaration of Independence\, one of 
 only twenty-six copies known today\, is the centerpiece of the exhibition.
  Printed immediately for distribution\, it is the source of all revolution
 ary era reprintings. The famous hand-written version was an official forma
 lity created later\, signed in August\, and stored away.Books\, pamphlets\
 , newspapers\, prints\, and letters allow viewers to explore key questions
  about this moment in time. How did a people proud to be in the British em
 pire come to believe independence was possible or even desirable? What ide
 as and historical events did they draw on to justify resistance to Great B
 ritain? What kinds of communication networks would be crucial for circulat
 ing the Declaration and countless other revolutionary documents throughout
  the colonies?This exhibition is part of America 250 at IU (https://go.iu.
 edu/america-250)\, a months-long civic festival offering our state expansi
 ve programming\, exhibits\, and events to honor our country's past while l
 ooking toward our shared future through common experiences for our campus 
 and community.
GEO:39.167909;-86.518974
LAST-MODIFIED:20260616T173211Z
LOCATION:LILLY LIBRARY
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2143431-the-declaration-of-independe
 nce-the-motives-the
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><i><span data-contrast="auto">The Declarat
 ion of Independence: The Motives\, The Moment</span></i><span data-contras
 t="auto">examines a crucial time in American history through the collectio
 ns of the Lilly Library. The first printing of the Declaration of Independ
 ence\, one of only twenty-six copies known today\, is the centerpiece of t
 he exhibition. Printed immediately for distribution\, it is the source of 
 all revolutionary era reprintings. The famous hand-written version was an 
 official formality created later\, signed in August\, and stored away.</sp
 an><span data-ccp-props="{}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="auto">Book
 s\, pamphlets\, newspapers\, prints\, and letters allow viewers to explore
  key questions about this moment in time. How did a people proud to be in 
 the British empire come to believe independence was possible or even desir
 able? What ideas and historical events did they draw on to justify resista
 nce to Great Britain? What kinds of communication networks would be crucia
 l for circulating the Declaration and countless other revolutionary docume
 nts throughout the colonies?</span><span data-ccp-props="{}"></span></p><h
 r /><p><span data-contrast="auto">This exhibition is part of <a href="http
 s://go.iu.edu/america-250">America 250 at IU</a>\, a months-long civic fes
 tival offering our state expansive programming\, exhibits\, and events to 
 honor our country's past while looking toward our shared future through co
 mmon experiences for our campus and community.</span></p><p><span data-con
 trast="auto"><picture class="lw_image lw_image29248  lw_align_center lw_bl
 ock lw_column_width_half"><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://events
 .iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/500/height/499/29248_America250-bloomingt
 on.rev.1765915309.webp 1x" data-origin="responsive"/><source type="image/p
 ng" srcset="https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/500/height/499/
 29248_America250-bloomington.rev.1765915309.png 1x" data-origin="responsiv
 e"/><img width="500" height="499" alt="" data-alt="" data-decoration="true
 " src="https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/500/height/499/29248
 _America250-bloomington.rev.1765915309.png" data-max-w="729" data-max-h="7
 27" loading="lazy" data-optimized="true"/></picture></span></p>
