X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Eskenazi School of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2344753-homeschool-day-light-and-chemistry-pm-session", "Architecture + Design": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2344753-homeschool-day-light-and-chemistry-pm-session", "Eskenazi Museum of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/2344753-homeschool-day-light-and-chemistry-pm-session"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 11": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2344753-homeschool-day-light-and-chemistry-pm-session"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_11
SUMMARY:Homeschool Day: Light and Chemistry (PM Session)
DTSTART:20261210T180000Z
DTEND:20261210T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260716T121542Z
UID:20261210T180000Z-2352814@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20261210T180000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1081,1081/31448_HSD-FullColor.rev.1783430812.png
DESCRIPTION:Through hands-on experiments with viewfinders\, pinhole camera
 s\, and cyanotype photograms\, students will discover how photography can 
 document history\, reflect change\, and draw inspiration from nature. From
  framing a scene to harnessing the power of sunlight\, we'll investigate h
 ow images are made and what they can communicate. Join us to experiment\, 
 observe\, and create your own light-powered photographs!  Program designed
  by our licensed art educator for students in grades K-12.Know Before You 
 Go:  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the m
 useum at 1 pm. Together\, we'll drop off personal items before exploring t
 he galleries. After seeing artworks that will inspire our project\, we'll 
 head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our own masterpi
 eces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!  Strollers are welcome. Chaperone 
 required. We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adult for every
  6 children.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20260716T161542Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2344753-homeschool-day-light-and-che
 mistry-pm-session
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Through hands-on experiments with viewfi
 nders\, pinhole cameras\, and cyanotype photograms\, students will discove
 r how photography can document history\, reflect change\, and draw inspira
 tion from nature. From framing a scene to harnessing the power of sunlight
 \, we'll investigate how images are made and what they can communicate. Jo
 in us to experiment\, observe\, and create your own light-powered photogra
 phs!</p><p>  Program designed by our licensed art educator for students in
  grades K-12.</p><p><strong>Know Before You Go:</strong></p><p>  Meet us i
 n the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the museum at 1 pm.
  Together\, we'll drop off personal items before exploring the galleries. 
 After seeing artworks that will inspire our project\, we'll head back to t
 he Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our own masterpieces! Don't fo
 rget to dress for a mess!</p><p>  Strollers are welcome. <strong>Chaperone
  required.</strong> We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adult
  for every 6 children.</p>
