BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Browncounty": "https://browncounty.com/events/rare-earth/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:browncounty
SUMMARY:Rare Earth
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270124T010000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270124T010000
DTSTAMP:20261019T150236Z
UID:MEC-220edb4c17f2cf1e263db766a85695af@browncounty.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20270124T010000
SEQUENCE:3
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 10/2-300x240-11.jpeg
CATEGORIES:Entertainment,Live Music
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261019
DESCRIPTION:Celebrating 55 years of the iconic hit “I Just Want To Celeb
 rate\,” Motown’s token rock band Rare Earth will make a stop at the Br
 own County Music Center in Nashville\, Ind.\, on Saturday\, January 23\, 2
 027.\nHailing from Detroit\, Rare Earth were a band inspired by the Motor 
 City’s twin legacies in hard rock and soul. Their biggest hits saw them 
 covering classic songs of the past\, while their sound found a middle grou
 nd between full-bodied rhythm & blues and tough bar band rock & roll. The 
 band began in 1960 as the Sunliners and played in and around Detroit. In 1
 968 the group changed its name to one more reflective of the psychedelic a
 ge. Their tight musicianship found room for them to transform their songs 
 through extended jams\, with their biggest hit\, “Get Ready\,” often c
 locking in at 30 minutes in concert. Other hits included Temptations cover
  “(I Know) I’m Losing You\,” original hit single\, “Born to Wander
 \,” and iconic signature song\, “I Just Want To Celebrate.”\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261029
LOCATION:200 Maple Leaf Boulevard\, Nashville\, IN 47448
ORGANIZER;CN="Brown County Music Center":MAILTO:boxoffice@browncountymusic
 center.com
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/rare-earth/
X-SOURCE:Brown County Events
END:VEVENT
