BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events Livewhale 221": "https://events.iu.edu/bfca/event/2184882-jessie-maple-patton-day-in-bloomington-indiana"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_livewhale_221
SUMMARY:Jessie Maple Patton Day in Bloomington\, Indiana
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270202
DTSTAMP:20260124T102024Z
UID:20270201T050000Z-2184882@events.iu.edu__20270201
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/221/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,3200,2133/29728_Jessie_Maple_2020_Courtesy_of_Black_Black
 _Film_Center__Archive.rev.1769267314.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Culture and languages,Functions, fes
 tivals, and celebrations,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences,Perfor
 mances, shows, and films
DESCRIPTION:Will (Jessie Maple\, 1981) is the one of the earliest survivin
 g features directed by a Black American woman. The Black Film Center &amp\
 ; Archive has been a proud steward of the film elements\, and much more\, 
 since the acquisition of The Jessie Maple Collection (https://indiana.us17
 .list-manage.com/track/click?u=f603b0d14ab6059bea01fbc72&amp\;id=d44ee4851
 2&amp\;e=9b80f7f3db) in 2005. Having undergone a 4K restoration\, Will is 
 screening for audiences around the world! Now\, Jessie Maple's films are a
 lso available to watch from the comfort of your own home on Criterion Chan
 nel! Will is included as part of the Black Debutantes (https://indiana.us1
 7.list-manage.com/track/click?u=f603b0d14ab6059bea01fbc72&amp\;id=2d70d816
 f1&amp\;e=9b80f7f3db) lineup\, which is a "celebration of pioneering Black
  women who made an impact with their very first—and in some cases only
 —feature film." Twice is Nice (Jessie Maple\, 1989) is also available.  
 If you would like to research the Jessie Maple collection\, email us at bf
 ca@iu.edu (mailto:bfca@iu.edu) to schedule an appointment.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260126T134930Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/bfca/event/2184882-jessie-maple-patton-day-in-bl
 oomington-indiana
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><em>Will</em> (Jessie Maple\, 1981) is the
  one of the earliest surviving features directed by a Black American woman
 . The Black Film Center &amp\; Archive has been a proud steward of the fil
 m elements\, and much more\, since the acquisition of <a href="https://ind
 iana.us17.list-manage.com/track/click?u=f603b0d14ab6059bea01fbc72&amp\;id=
 d44ee48512&amp\;e=9b80f7f3db" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedi
 recturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en&amp\;q=https://indiana.us17.list
 -manage.com/track/click?u%3Df603b0d14ab6059bea01fbc72%26id%3Dd44ee48512%26
 e%3D9b80f7f3db&amp\;source=gmail&amp\;ust=1769353570196000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw
 3uI5Eb7-9LI3fQaigo1TyZ">The Jessie Maple Collection</a> in 2005. Having un
 dergone a 4K restoration\, <em>Will</em> is screening for audiences around
  the world! Now\, Jessie Maple's films are also available to watch from th
 e comfort of your own home on Criterion Channel! <em>Will</em> is included
  as part of the <a href="https://indiana.us17.list-manage.com/track/click?
 u=f603b0d14ab6059bea01fbc72&amp\;id=2d70d816f1&amp\;e=9b80f7f3db" target="
 _blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl
 =en&amp\;q=https://indiana.us17.list-manage.com/track/click?u%3Df603b0d14a
 b6059bea01fbc72%26id%3D2d70d816f1%26e%3D9b80f7f3db&amp\;source=gmail&amp\;
 ust=1769353570196000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw02d1WcXkcWQiNFwjqawp34">Black Debutant
 es</a> lineup\, which is a "celebration of pioneering Black women who made
  an impact with their very first—and in some cases only—feature film."
  <em>Twice is Nice</em> (Jessie Maple\, 1989) is also available.</p><p>  I
 f you would like to research the Jessie Maple collection\, email us at <a 
 href="mailto:bfca@iu.edu">bfca@iu.edu</a> to schedule an appointment.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ALL-DAY:1
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  bfca@iu.edu\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2184882
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/221/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,3200\,2133/29728_Jessie_Maple_2020_Courtesy_
 of_Black_Black_Film_Center__Archive.rev.1769267314.jpg
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:Jessie Maple with the BFCA projector.&#160\;
X-LIVEWHALE-REPEATS-UNTIL:3026-02-01 05:00:00
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  Join us each year on Jessie Maple Patton Day\, 
 as we keep her legacy alive!!\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
X-SOURCE:IU Black Film Center & Archive
END:VEVENT
